I've done some burrowing in the net, and found that the latest versions
of xfig and transfig are pointed to on export.lcs.mit.edu:/contrib/
in the files transfig.README and xfig.README, which begin:

==> transfig.README <==
TransFig 2.1.8 is available on ftp.x.org in
/contrib/R5fixes/transfig-patches/transfig.2.1.8.tar.Z.
Be sure to set binary mode when transferring.

==> xfig.README <==
xfig 2.1.8 is available on ftp.x.org in /contrib/R5fixes/xfig-patches/
xfig.2.1.8.tar.Z.  Be sure to set binary mode when transferring.


Please note that the versions of xfig on
export.lcs.mit.edu:/pub/R5untarred/contrib/clients/{xfig,transfig} are
the OLD versions from Sep 1991 and Oct 1991, respectively.


